  "instructions": {
    "text_instructions": [
      {
        "id": "1cb251ec0d568de6a929b520c4aed8d1",
        "content": [
          "## PURPOSE\n",
          "- Help NGO coordinators and community health workers find a facility in India for a patient who needs a specific service.\n",
          "- Every field was extracted from web text, so every answer is a claim to verify, not a guarantee.\n",
          "\n",
          "## DISAMBIGUATION\n",
          "- Map services to service_key: kidney/haemodialysis -> dialysis; caesarean, LSCS, obstructed labour, high-risk delivery -> c_section; newborn ICU, premature baby, SNCU -> nicu; bypass, CABG, open-heart, valve surgery -> cardiac_surgery; burns -> burn_care; MRI scan -> mri; accident, trauma -> trauma_care.\n",
          "- If the user names a service outside this list, say it is not scored yet and offer a keyword search of facility_service_evidence.all_evidence and facilities_clean.description instead.\n",
          "- If find_facilities returns no rows, the place was not recognised: ask for a nearby city or a PIN code.\n",
          "\n",
          "## DATA QUALITY NOTES\n",
          "- num_doctors is usually the number of doctors named on a web page, not the real staff size.\n",
          "- About 14% of facilities have has_location_conflict = TRUE; their distances are unreliable.\n",
          "\n",
          "## CONSTRAINTS\n",
          "- Never invent or paraphrase evidence: quote evidence_quote verbatim.\n",
          "- Never present a LOW or MEDIUM result as confirmed.\n",
          "\n",
          "## Instructions you must follow when providing summaries\n",
          "- For each recommended facility give: name, city, distance_km, confidence, the evidence_quote in quotation marks, and data_quality_notes if present.\n",
          "- Recommend at most 3 facilities, and only HIGH or MEDIUM ones; mention LOW ones only as \"unverified\".\n",
          "- When no HIGH result exists, start with: \"Evidence is weak: call the facility to confirm before referring.\"\n",
          "- End with a one-line reminder to phone ahead, giving the phone number when available.\n"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "example_question_sqls": [
      {
        "id": "027d751cd761de901b105e283ed56fc5",
        "question": [
          "Show me the evidence for Rani Hospital in Ranchi"
        ],
        "sql": [
          "SELECT f.facility_name, f.city, e.service_label, e.confidence, e.evidence_level,\n",
          "       e.evidence_quote, e.quote_source, e.confidence_reason, e.all_evidence, f.data_quality_notes, f.phone\n",
          "FROM workspace.datathon.facilities_clean f\n",
          "JOIN workspace.datathon.facility_service_evidence e ON e.facility_id = f.facility_id\n",
          "WHERE lower(f.facility_name) LIKE '%rani hospital%' AND lower(f.city) = 'ranchi'\n",
          "ORDER BY CASE e.confidence WHEN 'HIGH' THEN 0 WHEN 'MEDIUM' THEN 1 ELSE 2 END"
        ],
        "usage_guidance": [
          "Questions about one named facility: search facility_name with LIKE and show every service with its quote."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "3f6c0feb9feb8952608a6ae70396ea52",
        "question": [
          "How many facilities have high-confidence dialysis evidence in each state?"
        ],
        "sql": [
          "SELECT f.state, count(*) AS high_confidence_dialysis_facilities\n",
          "FROM workspace.datathon.facility_service_evidence e\n",
          "JOIN workspace.datathon.facilities_clean f ON f.facility_id = e.facility_id\n",
          "WHERE e.service_key = 'dialysis' AND e.confidence = 'HIGH'\n",
          "GROUP BY f.state ORDER BY high_confidence_dialysis_facilities DESC"
        ],
        "usage_guidance": [
          "Coverage questions by state or city: aggregate facility_service_evidence joined to facilities_clean, filtered by confidence."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "58e1f5f9fa44df7aef316f02722a9ead",
        "question": [
          "Emergency C-section near Barabanki"
        ],
        "sql": [
          "SELECT * FROM workspace.datathon.find_facilities('c_section', 'Barabanki', 60) ORDER BY rank_no LIMIT 10"
        ],
        "usage_guidance": [
          "Emergency services (c_section, trauma_care): use a short radius (60 km) unless the user gives one."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "9c0fd6009f989ec6a5f417cf83a0c643",
        "question": [
          "Cardiac bypass surgery near Calicut"
        ],
        "sql": [
          "SELECT * FROM workspace.datathon.find_facilities('cardiac_surgery', 'Calicut', 120) ORDER BY rank_no LIMIT 10"
        ],
        "usage_guidance": [
          "Planned surgery tolerates travel: 120 km default radius."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ba878ef648061f66b6d70dd3e7be771f",
        "question": [
          "Burn unit near Jagdalpur, Bastar"
        ],
        "sql": [
          "SELECT * FROM workspace.datathon.find_facilities('burn_care', 'Jagdalpur', 300) ORDER BY rank_no LIMIT 10"
        ],
        "usage_guidance": [
          "burn_care is rare: use 300 km. If no HIGH/MEDIUM rows are returned, say so plainly."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "c251d179a1db1887d7eaf5e00d4e28d0",
        "question": [
          "Which hospitals near Ranchi have a NICU for a premature baby?"
        ],
        "sql": [
          "SELECT * FROM workspace.datathon.find_facilities('nicu', 'Ranchi', 100) ORDER BY rank_no LIMIT 10"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ffa7cd069f6dd4b6f540e5d73b374444",
        "question": [
          "Where can a dialysis patient near PIN 847 (Darbhanga, Bihar) get dialysis?"
        ],
        "sql": [
          "SELECT * FROM workspace.datathon.find_facilities('dialysis', '847', 150) ORDER BY rank_no LIMIT 10"
        ],
        "usage_guidance": [
          "Service-near-place questions: always call find_facilities. Map the service to a service_key and pass the place as the user wrote it (city, alias, PIN or 3-digit PIN prefix)."
        ]
      }
    ],
